%N A399351 Number of independent vertex sets in the n X n projective plane graph.
%C A399351 The n X n projective plane graph is constructed from an n X n grid graph by adding edges connecting opposite vertices around the border of the grid. It is similar to the Moebius strip, but twists are in both horizontal and vertical directions.
%H A399351 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/IndependentVertexSet.html">Independent Vertex Set</a>.
%e A399351 a(1) = 1 counts only the empty set because a vertex with a loop cannot be included in an independent vertex set.
%e A399351 a(2) = 5 corresponds to the number of independent vertex sets in the complete graph on 4 vertices.
%Y A399351 Main diagonal of A399350.
